{
  "id": "contexts/switching/14_other_host_code",
  "topic": "contexts",
  "subtopic": "switching",
  "title": "Code other hosts compile",
  "summary": "A header's code that only another host compiles keeps its colors, outline, folds, links and hover",
  "prose": "`shared.h` defines `fast_path()` when `fast_host.cpp` includes it and `slow_path()` when `slow_host.cpp` does. Shown in the first host's context, the second branch is dimmed as inactive, yet it keeps its semantic colors, its outline entry, its folds and its include link, and hovering `slow_path` shows its declaration: clice's index holds every context of the header, and while the file is as it was saved, the answers take the other contexts' code from it.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "fast_host.cpp",
      "text": "#define FAST\n#define LIMIT 1\n#include \"shared.h\"\n\nint main() {\n    return fast_path();\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "scale.h",
      "text": "#pragma once\n#define SCALE 2\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "shared.h",
      "text": "#pragma once\n\n#ifdef FAST\ninline int fast_path() {\n    return LIMIT;\n}\n#else\n#include \"scale.h\"\n\ninline int slow_path() {\n    return LIMIT * SCALE;\n}\n#endif\n",
      "markers": [
        {
          "name": "slow",
          "begin": 108,
          "end": 108,
          "range": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
